adjudication.rationale:
Yes. In `EventManager.createAllCalendarEvents`, when `event.destinationCalendar` is a non-empty array, it loops each `destination`. For destinations without `credentialId`, it does:

```ts
const destinationCalendarCredentials = this.calendarCredentials.filter(
  (c) => c.type === destination.integration
);
createdEvents = createdEvents.concat(
  await Promise.all(destinationCalendarCredentials.map(async (c) => await createEvent(c, event)))
);
```

If the array contains multiple `destination` entries with the same `integration` and no `credentialId`, this block runs multiple times and creates events for the same set of credentials repeatedly, producing duplicate calendar events. This duplication is directly introduced by the new array-based iteration (previously there was only a single `destinationCalendar`).
